  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">WILDLIFE LAW ENFORCEMENT IN GUINEA - GALF (Guine-Application de la Loi sur la Faune)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to assist the government of Guinea to increase wildlife law enforcement capacity, produce effective deterrents to the killing of elephant and other threatened wildlife, and monitor the illegtal wildlife trade and other activities detrimental to ape survival. The recipient will identify large-scale dealers in ivory and meat and provide evidence to support legal action against them; bring about the arrest of large-scale illegal wildlife traders; ensure the prosecution of large-scale illegal wildlife traders, and raise public awareness of the increased enforcement of wildlife alw and the risks and peanlties for wildlife criminals.</narrative>
  </description>
